1
00:00:35,098 --> 00:00:36,599
‎ATSUSHI MATSUYAMA - CUSTOMS OFFICER

2
00:00:36,683 --> 00:00:38,852
Looks pretty rough over there…

3
00:00:39,853 --> 00:00:42,397
-It's not gonna taste like my homemade.
-Passport, please. Your passport, please.

4
00:00:48,152 --> 00:00:50,905
‎RAN FUKAZAWA - CHIEF HEARING OFFICER

5
00:01:20,351 --> 00:01:23,146
Matsuyama, let that man through.

6
00:01:26,566 --> 00:01:28,067
IMMIGRATION OFFICER (MINISTRY OF JUSTICE)
AKIHIKO SEIKE

7
00:01:28,151 --> 00:01:29,611
Let him through before he suspects us.

8
00:01:47,295 --> 00:01:49,214
Was it really all right to let him pass?

9
00:01:49,297 --> 00:01:50,757
It's okay.

10
00:01:58,223 --> 00:02:00,558
"That thing" has happened.

11
00:02:14,072 --> 00:02:15,865
No more bets.

12
00:02:50,775 --> 00:02:52,777
These are this week's earnings.

13
00:02:57,448 --> 00:02:59,033
Police, don't move!

14
00:02:59,117 --> 00:02:59,993
Hey!

15
00:03:00,076 --> 00:03:02,996
-Hurry!
-Don't touch anything!

16
00:03:03,079 --> 00:03:05,665
Don't run! Hey!

17
00:03:07,750 --> 00:03:09,002
Don't move!

18
00:03:09,544 --> 00:03:12,672
So this is where
the underground casino was. Okay.

19
00:03:12,755 --> 00:03:14,882
Thank you for leading us here.

20
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:22,265
So that man was the operator
of an underground casino?

21
00:03:22,348 --> 00:03:24,600
And that's why he was
intentionally let through.

22
00:03:24,684 --> 00:03:26,519
He spotted it in that single moment.

23
00:03:26,602 --> 00:03:28,896
Chief Hearing Officer Fukazawa
really is amazing.

24
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:32,233
If we had stopped him at the gate,
it probably wouldn't have led to a raid.

25
00:03:32,316 --> 00:03:34,110
Still working?

26
00:03:34,193 --> 00:03:36,321
We've got one more push.

27
00:03:36,404 --> 00:03:38,031
Four tempura soba and three duck nanban.

28
00:03:38,114 --> 00:03:39,032
Okay.

29
00:03:39,115 --> 00:03:41,075
And inari sushi as well, please.

30
00:03:41,159 --> 00:03:44,454
-I'm sorry. The inari sushi is sold out.
-What…

31
00:03:44,537 --> 00:03:46,372
Look, her…

32
00:03:47,081 --> 00:03:48,750
She ate all of it.

33
00:03:48,833 --> 00:03:50,043
All of it?

34
00:03:50,126 --> 00:03:51,919
I think she ate about ten pieces.

35
00:03:52,003 --> 00:03:53,046
Coming.

36
00:03:53,796 --> 00:03:56,758
-Oh my…
-That will be 2,500 yen.

37
00:04:08,603 --> 00:04:10,396
-Do you have a parking ticket?
-Yes.

38
00:04:12,565 --> 00:04:14,776
KUUKYO

39
00:04:24,410 --> 00:04:25,495
‎KANTO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT TERMINAL 2

40
00:04:32,085 --> 00:04:33,836
Well, I'm heading off.

41
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:36,631
Hey, are you sure I shouldn't
come with you to the airport?

42
00:04:36,714 --> 00:04:38,591
It's fine, it's fine.

43
00:04:39,634 --> 00:04:41,844
He ended up not coming home after all.

44
00:04:41,928 --> 00:04:43,096
That's the same as always.

45
00:04:43,179 --> 00:04:45,014
‎MAYUMI FUKAZAWA - FUKAZAWA'S WIFE

46
00:04:45,098 --> 00:04:47,225
Even though his daughter is leaving
to study abroad today.

47
00:04:47,308 --> 00:04:49,352
It's fine, really.

48
00:04:49,435 --> 00:04:51,020
I'll tell him he should at least
see you off.

49
00:04:51,104 --> 00:04:52,647
I told you, it's fine.

50
00:04:52,730 --> 00:04:54,107
I'm already 17.

51
00:04:56,109 --> 00:04:58,152
Besides, he's probably busy anyway.

52
00:04:58,236 --> 00:05:00,029
What is he, an inspection officer?

53
00:05:00,113 --> 00:05:04,200
An immigration inspector. And he's
quite high up among them, you know?

54
00:05:05,785 --> 00:05:09,205
Shouldn't high-up people
have more free time?

55
00:05:12,417 --> 00:05:14,210
See you, Dad.

56
00:05:20,466 --> 00:05:22,593
-Take care.
-Goodbye.

57
00:05:28,141 --> 00:05:31,102
What? You did the raid yesterday, Iuchi?

58
00:05:31,185 --> 00:05:32,061
That's right.

59
00:05:32,937 --> 00:05:37,066
Man, it was a tough case.

60
00:05:37,150 --> 00:05:39,068
You're straight on the promotion track.

61
00:05:39,152 --> 00:05:41,112
Hey there, future Superintendent General.

62
00:05:41,696 --> 00:05:43,948
Though it was thanks
to Chief Hearing Officer Fukazawa.

63
00:05:44,031 --> 00:05:44,907
Actually,

64
00:05:45,575 --> 00:05:49,787
one female operator from the casino
is currently on the run.

65
00:05:49,871 --> 00:05:52,373
-What, she hasn't been caught yet?
-Yes.

66
00:05:52,456 --> 00:05:54,333
Iuchi, you're talking too much!

67
00:05:57,253 --> 00:06:00,214
Please be very cautious
for the time being.

68
00:06:00,798 --> 00:06:02,049
Understood, Superintendent General.

69
00:06:04,802 --> 00:06:07,138
Following last night's raid,
new information has come in

70
00:06:07,221 --> 00:06:09,015
from the Metropolitan Police Department.

71
00:06:09,098 --> 00:06:11,142
It seems that a large shipment
of illegal drugs

72
00:06:11,225 --> 00:06:14,437
worth several hundred million yen will be
brought in through this airport shortly.

73
00:06:15,313 --> 00:06:18,107
-Have you identified the courier?
-Not yet.

74
00:06:18,191 --> 00:06:21,068
However, there's a high probability
they hold a Japanese passport.

75
00:06:21,152 --> 00:06:22,945
A Japanese national…

76
00:06:23,029 --> 00:06:25,615
There might be
a major organization behind this.

77
00:06:25,698 --> 00:06:27,658
If there's even
the slightest suspicious detail,

78
00:06:27,742 --> 00:06:30,328
route them for inspection
regardless of nationality.

79
00:06:30,411 --> 00:06:31,245
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

80
00:06:31,329 --> 00:06:34,207
We must stop those drugs coming in.

81
00:06:34,290 --> 00:06:36,792
Right. We won't let even
a single gram pass.

82
00:06:36,876 --> 00:06:38,753
Not even a single milligram.

83
00:06:38,836 --> 00:06:39,795
-So specific.
-Okay,

84
00:07:08,115 --> 00:07:10,952
-Go ahead.
-I'll check your luggage.

85
00:07:12,537 --> 00:07:13,538
Go ahead.

86
00:07:22,088 --> 00:07:23,548
This is quite large.

87
00:07:23,631 --> 00:07:25,883
It was cheap, so I just bought it.

88
00:07:25,967 --> 00:07:27,635
It would make
a good souvenir for my niece.

89
00:07:39,021 --> 00:07:40,481
This doesn't feel like cotton.

90
00:07:41,107 --> 00:07:44,652
-It's made overseas, after all.
-That's just how it's made.

91
00:07:47,697 --> 00:07:48,781
I'm going to open this up.

92
00:08:05,423 --> 00:08:07,967
These are cartridges
for electronic cigarettes.

93
00:08:08,050 --> 00:08:12,346
Nicotine-containing electronic cigarettes
have a set limit for personal importation.

94
00:08:13,180 --> 00:08:15,725
This exceeds the regulated amount.

95
00:08:16,601 --> 00:08:18,144
What, really?

96
00:08:18,227 --> 00:08:20,313
-We had no idea.
-Yes.

97
00:08:20,396 --> 00:08:22,315
Do you have
an import confirmation certificate?

98
00:08:22,398 --> 00:08:26,068
Forget it. We can just pay
the extra tax, right?

99
00:08:26,152 --> 00:08:27,903
How much is it? How much!

100
00:08:27,987 --> 00:08:30,239
I was just a bit careless!

101
00:08:32,617 --> 00:08:34,410
You were careless enough to sew it in?

102
00:08:36,329 --> 00:08:37,496
Next person, please.

103
00:08:37,580 --> 00:08:38,497
‎SARA NATORI - IMMIGRATION OFFICER

104
00:08:39,081 --> 00:08:39,957
Over here.

105
00:08:40,708 --> 00:08:41,876
I'll take your passport.

106
00:08:48,591 --> 00:08:50,593
IMMIGRATION PASSPORT READING SYSTEM

107
00:08:52,803 --> 00:08:54,930
Please proceed.

108
00:08:55,014 --> 00:08:57,350
Do you have anything to declare?

109
00:08:57,433 --> 00:08:58,434
No.

110
00:09:00,603 --> 00:09:02,730
Well then, welcome home.

111
00:09:04,565 --> 00:09:05,566
Well…

112
00:09:08,152 --> 00:09:11,280
That neck pillow seems quite light.

113
00:09:12,114 --> 00:09:13,574
It's made of urethane.

114
00:09:14,116 --> 00:09:15,785
May I take a look at it?

115
00:09:25,169 --> 00:09:27,588
This tag says it is made of gel.

116
00:09:47,024 --> 00:09:49,610
-And this is?
-T-tea leaves!

117
00:09:49,694 --> 00:09:50,778
Herbal tea, herbal tea!

118
00:09:50,861 --> 00:09:54,073
No it is not. It's dried cannabis.

119
00:09:56,409 --> 00:09:57,910
Are you serious?

120
00:09:58,577 --> 00:10:01,580
Do you normally check this carefully?

121
00:10:01,664 --> 00:10:05,209
Our inspectors certainly do.

122
00:10:28,441 --> 00:10:31,402
I'LL DEFINITELY BE THERE, WAIT FOR ME

123
00:10:33,112 --> 00:10:35,781
You really don't have to force yourself.

124
00:10:36,574 --> 00:10:39,577
-Non-stop confiscations today.
-It's a turbulent morning.

125
00:10:40,286 --> 00:10:44,248
That just means Gate 24
is doing its job right.

126
00:10:44,331 --> 00:10:45,666
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

127
00:10:46,333 --> 00:10:47,960
What about the drugs we're looking for?

128
00:10:48,043 --> 00:10:50,296
Nothing matching that description
has been found yet.

129
00:10:50,379 --> 00:10:51,547
I see.

130
00:10:52,214 --> 00:10:53,215
Oh, that's right.

131
00:10:53,299 --> 00:10:55,342
Your daughter
is leaving to study abroad today, right?

132
00:10:55,426 --> 00:10:56,260
Yes.

133
00:10:56,343 --> 00:10:58,220
Are you going to see her off?

134
00:10:58,304 --> 00:11:01,223
If I can go during my break.

135
00:11:01,307 --> 00:11:03,100
You have to go.

136
00:11:03,184 --> 00:11:05,102
She'll be mad at you if you don't.

137
00:11:05,186 --> 00:11:08,272
Man, I hope she is just mad.

138
00:11:22,536 --> 00:11:25,164
The afternoon flights are finally done.

139
00:11:25,247 --> 00:11:27,333
Good job, everyone.

140
00:11:27,416 --> 00:11:28,876
-Shall we clean up?
-Yes.

141
00:11:28,959 --> 00:11:30,419
-Yes.
-Ah, wait!

142
00:11:41,096 --> 00:11:42,306
Go ahead.

143
00:11:51,482 --> 00:11:54,860
-This is our last passenger.
-Okay.

144
00:12:01,909 --> 00:12:02,785
‎CHIKA KUMAGAWA - GROUND STAFF

145
00:12:02,868 --> 00:12:05,120
-Allow me to assist you.
-Thank you.

146
00:12:07,581 --> 00:12:09,250
Right over here, please.

147
00:12:14,713 --> 00:12:17,216
-I'll take a look at your passport.
-Yes.

148
00:12:26,850 --> 00:12:28,561
Yuma Takase.

149
00:12:28,644 --> 00:12:30,437
Returning from South Oserna, I see.

150
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:32,439
Yes.

151
00:12:33,857 --> 00:12:36,986
This one says Misaki Takase.

152
00:12:38,028 --> 00:12:39,238
My wife.

153
00:12:41,156 --> 00:12:42,324
She's here.

154
00:12:43,993 --> 00:12:45,703
My condolences.

155
00:12:47,329 --> 00:12:48,414
Go ahead.

156
00:12:53,335 --> 00:12:56,755
-Are those your wife's remains?
-Yes.

157
00:12:57,840 --> 00:13:02,428
During our trip, she suddenly collapsed
at the hotel, and just like that…

158
00:13:04,013 --> 00:13:05,556
I see.

159
00:13:06,515 --> 00:13:09,184
You can leave your luggage here.
Please proceed.

160
00:13:11,353 --> 00:13:12,813
Oh…

161
00:13:15,566 --> 00:13:16,734
Here…

162
00:13:28,329 --> 00:13:31,540
Here, this is the death certificate

163
00:13:31,624 --> 00:13:34,084
and the cremation certificate.

164
00:13:34,168 --> 00:13:35,002
And this is--

165
00:13:35,085 --> 00:13:37,880
-You don't need those documents here.
-Huh?

166
00:13:39,590 --> 00:13:42,301
-I'm sorry.
-Are you all right?

167
00:13:42,384 --> 00:13:44,178
I'll pick them up.

168
00:13:44,261 --> 00:13:45,804
Ah, I'm sorry.

169
00:14:02,738 --> 00:14:05,157
Ah, I'm sorry. That's mine as well.
Thank you.

170
00:14:19,046 --> 00:14:22,299
Well then, may I pass through?

171
00:14:22,383 --> 00:14:24,093
Of course. Right?

172
00:14:24,843 --> 00:14:26,261
Um…

173
00:14:28,430 --> 00:14:32,393
May we inspect your luggage a bit further?

174
00:14:33,018 --> 00:14:34,770
-What?
-Mori?

175
00:14:35,938 --> 00:14:38,190
I'm sorry. Please wait just a moment.

176
00:14:38,273 --> 00:14:39,900
Mori, over here for a second.

177
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:44,196
Natori. I'm sorry.

178
00:14:50,202 --> 00:14:52,538
What do you mean, inspect the luggage?

179
00:14:52,621 --> 00:14:54,164
There was something that bothered me.

180
00:14:55,082 --> 00:14:58,502
Takase just lost his wife, you know?

181
00:14:58,585 --> 00:14:59,837
I understand.

182
00:14:59,920 --> 00:15:02,464
However, Chief Hearing Officer Fukazawa
also said

183
00:15:02,548 --> 00:15:06,093
to route anyone for inspection if there's
even the slightest suspicion.

184
00:15:06,176 --> 00:15:08,554
That's true, but…

185
00:15:09,346 --> 00:15:12,099
Just now, I saw inside the luggage,

186
00:15:12,182 --> 00:15:14,476
and the clothes in there
were all summer clothes.

187
00:15:14,560 --> 00:15:16,770
Well, of course. It's summer right now.

188
00:15:16,854 --> 00:15:19,481
South Oserna is in
the Southern Hemisphere.

189
00:15:20,190 --> 00:15:21,483
It is winter there right now.

190
00:15:23,110 --> 00:15:25,487
And yet, there wasn't
a single piece of winter clothing.

191
00:15:26,113 --> 00:15:28,032
Yes. It is strange.

192
00:15:28,115 --> 00:15:30,909
He might have disposed
of them over there, right?

193
00:15:30,993 --> 00:15:33,037
-Furthermore…
-There's more?

194
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:36,832
Takase ate a meal
at the airport before departure.

195
00:15:37,416 --> 00:15:39,334
-A meal?
-How do you know that?

196
00:15:40,085 --> 00:15:41,920
I picked up a receipt.

197
00:15:42,421 --> 00:15:47,384
One cup of coffee, a large pasta,
a club sandwich, a hamburg steak,

198
00:15:47,468 --> 00:15:50,763
-and cheesecake.
-No, no.

199
00:15:50,846 --> 00:15:53,057
Even if you're grieving,
you still get hungry.

200
00:15:53,766 --> 00:15:58,771
Or rather, maybe he hadn't had time
to eat anything up until then.

201
00:15:58,854 --> 00:16:01,231
T-that may be so.

202
00:16:01,315 --> 00:16:03,984
-However--
-It's not that I'm saying

203
00:16:04,068 --> 00:16:08,363
I feel bad for Takase, so don't
inspect him, or anything like that.

204
00:16:08,447 --> 00:16:09,406
It's just that

205
00:16:10,115 --> 00:16:15,079
placing an additional burden on him
without clear evidence doesn't feel right.

206
00:16:16,955 --> 00:16:18,082
Yes.

207
00:16:18,165 --> 00:16:21,919
Well, it's true that each point
is weak on its own as evidence,

208
00:16:22,002 --> 00:16:24,213
but it's also true that
strange details are adding up.

209
00:16:28,842 --> 00:16:31,053
Shall we check, just to be sure?

210
00:16:33,013 --> 00:16:34,890
Just to be sure.

211
00:16:40,729 --> 00:16:42,397
Excuse me.

212
00:16:47,277 --> 00:16:49,780
How much longer will this take?

213
00:16:51,198 --> 00:16:53,283
We are very sorry.

214
00:17:21,687 --> 00:17:23,897
May I check that bag as well?

215
00:17:27,442 --> 00:17:28,318
Yes.

216
00:17:29,486 --> 00:17:31,029
Thank you.

217
00:17:46,879 --> 00:17:48,922
This medicine hasn't been declared.

218
00:17:51,091 --> 00:17:53,886
I'm sorry. They're sleeping pills.

219
00:17:54,469 --> 00:17:56,972
Were they prescribed by a local hospital?

220
00:17:57,055 --> 00:18:02,019
Yes. Ever since my wife passed away,
I haven't been able to sleep at all.

221
00:18:03,979 --> 00:18:06,815
Okay then, please complete
the declaration procedure later.

222
00:18:06,899 --> 00:18:08,317
Yes.

223
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:10,611
I'm truly sorry.

224
00:18:16,408 --> 00:18:17,784
‎GATE 24 - SECONDARY ROOM

225
00:18:17,868 --> 00:18:21,330
For now, I'm relieved that
nothing dangerous turned up.

226
00:18:21,413 --> 00:18:22,456
‎Yeah.

227
00:18:22,539 --> 00:18:24,166
Are you still investigating?

228
00:18:24,249 --> 00:18:26,126
Was there anything suspicious?

229
00:18:26,210 --> 00:18:29,129
No. Mori, there's no problem, right?

230
00:18:29,213 --> 00:18:31,048
-No.
-Well then,

231
00:18:31,131 --> 00:18:32,841
-that concludes--
-Something should be here,

232
00:18:32,925 --> 00:18:34,968
but it is missing.

233
00:18:37,763 --> 00:18:40,766
-Mori, there's no problem, right?
-No.

234
00:18:40,849 --> 00:18:43,477
-Well then, that concludes--
-Something should be here,

235
00:18:43,560 --> 00:18:45,312
-but it is missing.
-What?

236
00:18:49,608 --> 00:18:52,110
-Contact lenses?
-Yes.

237
00:18:52,194 --> 00:18:54,947
They were in the deceased wife's luggage,

238
00:18:55,030 --> 00:18:58,283
but the prescription here is minus 7.00.

239
00:18:58,367 --> 00:19:00,953
Huh, that's about the same as mine.

240
00:19:01,036 --> 00:19:02,829
Endo, you wear contact lenses?

241
00:19:02,913 --> 00:19:05,415
Yes, if I take them out, I can't see.

242
00:19:05,499 --> 00:19:07,542
That's why I always carry glasses around.

243
00:19:07,626 --> 00:19:10,045
-I see.
-True, they aren't there.

244
00:19:11,255 --> 00:19:14,383
Yes, there are no glasses.

245
00:19:14,466 --> 00:19:18,845
If traveling, it would be natural
to bring them as a spare.

246
00:19:18,929 --> 00:19:21,473
Maybe he lost them somewhere?

247
00:19:21,556 --> 00:19:24,601
Besides, does him not having glasses
imply something bad?

248
00:19:25,394 --> 00:19:26,979
That, I do not know.

249
00:19:28,647 --> 00:19:30,148
Let's just let him go already.

250
00:19:31,108 --> 00:19:35,862
Takase lost his partner
and hasn't been able to sleep.

251
00:19:41,493 --> 00:19:42,869
What's wrong?

252
00:19:43,453 --> 00:19:46,623
Takase was drinking coffee
before coming here.

253
00:19:46,707 --> 00:19:49,459
-And it was a Robusta blend.
-Robusta?

254
00:19:49,543 --> 00:19:52,671
Yes. A bean with a strong bitter taste
and high caffeine content.

255
00:19:52,754 --> 00:19:56,967
Would someone suffering from insomnia
drink such coffee right before boarding?

256
00:19:57,050 --> 00:19:59,011
Yes. It is strange.

257
00:20:00,929 --> 00:20:02,472
Feels like there are

258
00:20:03,223 --> 00:20:04,766
a lot of small catches, huh?

259
00:20:04,850 --> 00:20:10,063
But it's not decisively suspicious, is it?

260
00:20:10,605 --> 00:20:14,651
Everyone, please be careful
in dealing with the bereaved man.

261
00:20:14,735 --> 00:20:17,154
It affects the credibility
of the entire gate.

262
00:20:17,237 --> 00:20:19,740
I think it's best to stop here as well.

263
00:20:29,541 --> 00:20:34,629
I will guide passengers on EuroSky Airways
Flight ESA235 bound for London.

264
00:20:34,713 --> 00:20:36,840
Check-in is now beginning.

265
00:20:36,923 --> 00:20:40,093
Please have your passport ready
and proceed to the check-in counter.

266
00:20:40,177 --> 00:20:41,678
TO LONDON

267
00:20:49,728 --> 00:20:52,356
-Ah, Dad!
-Here, take this.

268
00:20:52,439 --> 00:20:53,899
Okay, thank you.

269
00:20:54,816 --> 00:20:56,526
Well, I'm off now.

270
00:20:56,610 --> 00:20:59,696
Miss, do you know where
the check-in counter is?

271
00:21:01,114 --> 00:21:03,575
Yes, I'm fine.

272
00:21:16,671 --> 00:21:22,344
I'M GOING SOON, OKAY?

273
00:21:30,185 --> 00:21:32,229
There was nothing in the luggage, right?

274
00:21:32,312 --> 00:21:33,522
No.

275
00:21:33,605 --> 00:21:37,484
-In that case, we should stop here--
-Well…

276
00:21:38,318 --> 00:21:42,155
There is still one place
we haven't checked.

277
00:21:59,256 --> 00:22:01,466
Wait, Mori.

278
00:22:01,550 --> 00:22:04,428
-You don't mean…
-There's no way we could do that.

279
00:22:04,511 --> 00:22:06,972
If we handle this wrong,
it will become a really big problem.

280
00:22:07,055 --> 00:22:08,598
We must consider his feelings.

281
00:22:09,641 --> 00:22:12,144
If it were me, I might never forgive it.

282
00:22:12,894 --> 00:22:16,648
Demanding to inspect the urn
where my wife rests…

283
00:22:21,069 --> 00:22:23,363
What do you think, Matsuyama?

284
00:22:23,447 --> 00:22:24,614
Are you against it?

285
00:22:27,325 --> 00:22:30,996
Actually, there's one thing bothering me.

286
00:22:33,415 --> 00:22:35,041
Earlier, Takase…

287
00:22:41,006 --> 00:22:43,717
It looked like he intentionally
drew our eyes to that bag.

288
00:22:44,676 --> 00:22:47,596
-Intentionally?
-I was bothered by that as well.

289
00:22:47,679 --> 00:22:50,765
Could there have been something else
he didn't want inspected?

290
00:22:50,849 --> 00:22:52,350
Meaning…

291
00:22:55,937 --> 00:22:58,940
But if we don't find anything in it…

292
00:22:59,649 --> 00:23:01,568
Takase will probably get angry at us.

293
00:23:02,194 --> 00:23:04,905
He might yell at us and hold a grudge.

294
00:23:04,988 --> 00:23:07,115
Oh, no, come on…

295
00:23:08,450 --> 00:23:11,786
But that's

296
00:23:13,079 --> 00:23:14,873
part of our job as well.

297
00:23:18,752 --> 00:23:19,711
Right?

298
00:23:21,546 --> 00:23:22,589
Yes.

299
00:23:24,090 --> 00:23:25,217
Hayami?

300
00:23:34,559 --> 00:23:37,687
COMING NOW, SORRY I'M LATE

301
00:23:46,488 --> 00:23:47,697
She's mad, huh?

302
00:23:56,289 --> 00:23:57,290
I'm almost there.

303
00:23:57,374 --> 00:24:00,210
Ah, this is Seike.

304
00:24:01,962 --> 00:24:05,090
-What's up?
-Well,

305
00:24:05,173 --> 00:24:09,719
we've decided to inspect
a passenger's urn.

306
00:24:12,138 --> 00:24:16,768
Since it's a serious matter, we would
like you to be present as well.

307
00:24:19,187 --> 00:24:20,647
What is he doing?

308
00:24:20,730 --> 00:24:22,732
‎…please try again later…

309
00:24:26,611 --> 00:24:27,570
Understood.

310
00:24:28,863 --> 00:24:29,990
I'll be right there.

311
00:24:42,252 --> 00:24:43,461
Let's go.

312
00:24:44,963 --> 00:24:46,381
Excuse me.

313
00:24:47,132 --> 00:24:49,592
I am Chief Hearing Officer Fukazawa.

314
00:24:51,386 --> 00:24:52,387
Fukazawa?

315
00:24:53,596 --> 00:24:55,307
Takase?

316
00:24:55,390 --> 00:24:58,143
-Do you know each other?
-Yes.

317
00:24:58,226 --> 00:24:59,894
We're mountain-climbing friends.

318
00:24:59,978 --> 00:25:03,189
We paired up as buddies and tried
to summit together many times.

319
00:25:03,273 --> 00:25:04,733
I see.

320
00:25:05,608 --> 00:25:08,778
Fukazawa helped me
on the mountains many times.

321
00:25:12,574 --> 00:25:15,869
You were reckless,
and I had to bail you out.

322
00:25:20,081 --> 00:25:21,541
I heard what happened.

323
00:25:23,001 --> 00:25:26,880
I heard about Misaki. It's unfortunate.

324
00:25:29,090 --> 00:25:30,050
Yes.

325
00:25:32,844 --> 00:25:35,680
Misaki often came
to the mountaineering club as well.

326
00:25:36,389 --> 00:25:37,974
She wasn't good with the cold.

327
00:25:39,434 --> 00:25:42,312
She always said she hated snow mountains

328
00:25:42,395 --> 00:25:45,231
and would wait at the mountain lodge.

329
00:25:45,899 --> 00:25:47,484
Was that so?

330
00:25:48,860 --> 00:25:50,570
You remember well.

331
00:25:52,280 --> 00:25:55,492
She was someone who valued life.

332
00:25:56,826 --> 00:25:59,329
Misaki would be pleased to hear that too.

333
00:26:03,750 --> 00:26:07,462
-Hey, Takase--
-Um, please, let me go home already.

334
00:26:08,588 --> 00:26:10,632
I presented my documents and passport.

335
00:26:10,715 --> 00:26:12,634
I showed all my luggage.

336
00:26:13,385 --> 00:26:14,928
What else are you doubting?

337
00:26:16,513 --> 00:26:17,514
Finally,

338
00:26:19,516 --> 00:26:21,976
I would like to inspect that.

339
00:26:27,941 --> 00:26:29,234
Are you serious?

340
00:26:32,821 --> 00:26:35,657
The person inside here
is Misaki, you know?

341
00:26:36,533 --> 00:26:39,494
-I am very sorry.
-Fukazawa!

342
00:26:41,579 --> 00:26:46,543
To ensure it isn't touched
more than necessary, I will be present.

343
00:27:43,099 --> 00:27:44,184
I'll open it.

344
00:28:00,825 --> 00:28:02,660
They're quite fine.

345
00:28:02,744 --> 00:28:06,122
Depending on the country,
they crush human remains finely.

346
00:28:11,544 --> 00:28:12,837
Visually, there are no abnormalities.

347
00:28:31,356 --> 00:28:33,107
Nothing abnormal on the X-ray either.

348
00:28:58,967 --> 00:29:00,844
No drug reaction either.

349
00:29:08,476 --> 00:29:12,146
Even though it was part of my duties,
I hurt you and Misaki.

350
00:29:12,230 --> 00:29:15,733
I apologize from the bottom
of my heart. I am truly sorry.

351
00:29:18,987 --> 00:29:21,531
Fukazawa, please raise your head.

352
00:29:25,410 --> 00:29:28,496
Suspecting people is your job, after all.

353
00:29:29,163 --> 00:29:33,251
Nothing showed up,
so that's enough for me.

354
00:29:35,587 --> 00:29:39,090
Let me offer incense to her
next time I see you.

355
00:29:40,508 --> 00:29:43,344
Yes. Misaki will be happy too.

356
00:29:46,639 --> 00:29:47,849
Thank you for waiting.

357
00:29:49,267 --> 00:29:50,184
Thank you.

358
00:29:52,437 --> 00:29:53,354
Well then.

359
00:30:05,617 --> 00:30:06,659
Good work, everyone.

360
00:30:12,707 --> 00:30:14,250
-It's heartbreaking.
-Yes.

361
00:30:15,209 --> 00:30:17,879
Somehow, Takase not being mad at us
makes it even sadder.

362
00:31:06,970 --> 00:31:09,055
I will report to the higher-ups now.

363
00:31:09,138 --> 00:31:11,307
It couldn't be helped.
It was a necessary check.

364
00:31:11,391 --> 00:31:13,559
Even so, what the higher-ups will say…

365
00:31:13,643 --> 00:31:15,436
Oh, stop complaining!

366
00:31:15,520 --> 00:31:16,980
Just brace yourselves!

367
00:31:17,063 --> 00:31:18,815
Give me a break.
I'm the one they'll scold.

368
00:31:18,898 --> 00:31:20,733
Mori? What are you doing?

369
00:31:25,113 --> 00:31:26,823
Sorry, everyone.

370
00:31:28,574 --> 00:31:32,245
Didn't think I'd run into
an acquaintance on the job.

371
00:31:32,912 --> 00:31:34,497
Um…

372
00:31:34,580 --> 00:31:35,748
What's wrong?

373
00:31:36,541 --> 00:31:39,335
I met Takase's wife…

374
00:31:43,089 --> 00:31:44,507
yesterday.

375
00:31:44,590 --> 00:31:46,718
-Huh?
-His wife?

376
00:31:46,801 --> 00:31:48,177
What do you mean?

377
00:31:48,761 --> 00:31:53,224
First, please look at this.
It was among his wife's luggage.

378
00:31:53,850 --> 00:31:57,729
This was a coaster from a casino
named "Noir" in South Oserna.

379
00:31:58,521 --> 00:32:00,106
-A casino?
-Yes.

380
00:32:00,189 --> 00:32:03,943
However, I checked, and this establishment
doesn't have an operating license.

381
00:32:05,028 --> 00:32:07,739
-An underground casino?
-Most likely.

382
00:32:07,822 --> 00:32:12,118
Are you saying the Takase couple
went to that underground casino?

383
00:32:12,201 --> 00:32:14,412
It would explain why Misaki,
who is sensitive to the cold,

384
00:32:14,495 --> 00:32:18,291
went to South Oserna
without bringing winter clothes.

385
00:32:18,374 --> 00:32:20,293
She stayed in a casino the whole time.

386
00:32:20,376 --> 00:32:21,252
Yes.

387
00:32:22,003 --> 00:32:25,506
Could that be related
to Iuchi's information?

388
00:32:25,590 --> 00:32:26,758
Iuchi's?

389
00:32:26,841 --> 00:32:29,010
That a female underground
casino operator is on the run.

390
00:32:29,719 --> 00:32:32,513
-An operator?
-That, I do not know.

391
00:32:32,597 --> 00:32:36,017
However, yesterday, I saw something
at the airport's soba shop.

392
00:32:42,982 --> 00:32:45,610
A woman holding chips from this casino.

393
00:32:46,527 --> 00:32:47,779
That lady?

394
00:32:47,862 --> 00:32:49,572
How did you remember that so well?

395
00:32:49,655 --> 00:32:50,990
She ate ten pieces of inari sushi.

396
00:32:51,074 --> 00:32:53,659
-Ah, so that's why.
-A grudge over that inari sushi, huh?

397
00:32:54,243 --> 00:32:57,330
So, why do you think
that woman was Misaki?

398
00:32:57,413 --> 00:32:59,874
The casino is not the only reason.

399
00:33:00,666 --> 00:33:01,918
Look at this.

400
00:33:04,295 --> 00:33:07,507
This is a towel that was
in the wife's luggage.

401
00:33:08,091 --> 00:33:12,095
That woman also had a key case
with this exact same logo.

402
00:33:14,847 --> 00:33:16,516
It is a minor heavy metal band.

403
00:33:18,518 --> 00:33:24,482
-Then the lady at the soba shop was…
-Takase's wife?

404
00:33:24,565 --> 00:33:26,651
Yes. Looking at it that way,

405
00:33:26,734 --> 00:33:28,736
all the strange details connect.

406
00:33:29,403 --> 00:33:31,823
-Strange details?
-Ah.

407
00:33:31,906 --> 00:33:33,407
For example, this.

408
00:33:34,408 --> 00:33:36,661
In the wife's luggage,
there were slippers.

409
00:33:37,286 --> 00:33:40,039
However, there are no shoes
for outdoor wear.

410
00:33:40,123 --> 00:33:42,667
What was she wearing during the trip?

411
00:33:44,794 --> 00:33:48,214
No shoes or glasses
in the luggage, does that mean…

412
00:33:48,297 --> 00:33:50,716
Those are things necessary for driving.

413
00:33:50,800 --> 00:33:52,593
Yes, that is correct.

414
00:33:52,677 --> 00:33:55,930
Furthermore, at that time,
that woman presented a parking ticket.

415
00:33:56,013 --> 00:33:58,099
-Do you have a parking ticket?
-Yes.

416
00:33:58,182 --> 00:34:00,017
PARKING TICKET

417
00:34:00,101 --> 00:34:03,980
In other words, that woman
came to the airport by car.

418
00:34:05,148 --> 00:34:07,191
Perhaps even now,

419
00:34:07,275 --> 00:34:09,193
she might be driving somewhere.

420
00:34:23,916 --> 00:34:25,668
I borrowed this from the security center.

421
00:34:25,751 --> 00:34:27,795
It's CCTV footage
from around the soba shop yesterday.

422
00:34:32,717 --> 00:34:38,431
SOBA

423
00:34:45,855 --> 00:34:49,400
-That's…
-The inari sushi woman.

424
00:35:00,703 --> 00:35:02,538
-Iuchi…
-You know,

425
00:35:02,622 --> 00:35:06,125
I asked before, but could you not treat
the police like a handyman service?

426
00:35:06,209 --> 00:35:08,836
Sorry, future Superintendent General.

427
00:35:09,420 --> 00:35:11,547
Well, I'll forgive you this time.

428
00:35:11,631 --> 00:35:12,965
What, you will?

429
00:35:13,049 --> 00:35:14,800
What was the result of the inquiry?

430
00:35:14,884 --> 00:35:18,179
Is this person the female casino operator
you were talking about, Iuchi?

431
00:35:18,262 --> 00:35:20,014
No, she was unrelated to that.

432
00:35:20,097 --> 00:35:22,808
However, as a result
of facial recognition matching,

433
00:35:22,892 --> 00:35:25,686
it matched the passport photo
of Misaki Takase.

434
00:35:25,770 --> 00:35:29,357
-Then…
-This woman is Misaki Takase.

435
00:35:31,067 --> 00:35:35,196
-She's alive.
-Then, what was inside that urn?

436
00:35:35,279 --> 00:35:36,822
Where is Takase right now?

437
00:36:00,096 --> 00:36:01,722
-Let's go.
-Okay!

438
00:36:02,348 --> 00:36:03,432
Counselor!

439
00:36:04,141 --> 00:36:07,687
Information just came in
from South Oserna Airport.

440
00:36:08,271 --> 00:36:11,691
Misaki Takase is suspected of having left
using another person's passport.

441
00:36:11,774 --> 00:36:12,858
We thought so.

442
00:36:12,942 --> 00:36:15,194
Local authorities are also pursuing
her whereabouts. At this rate…

443
00:36:15,278 --> 00:36:18,698
At this rate, it could become
an international incident

444
00:36:18,781 --> 00:36:21,867
because you people
didn't catch that couple.

445
00:36:22,618 --> 00:36:25,538
Why didn't you inspect them
more thoroughly?

446
00:36:25,621 --> 00:36:28,332
If we had inspected them,
you would have complained anyway.

447
00:36:28,416 --> 00:36:31,002
-Did you say something?
-No, nothing.

448
00:36:31,085 --> 00:36:32,420
Um…

449
00:36:33,546 --> 00:36:37,425
Strictly speaking, the one that overlooked
Misaki Takase's illegal entry

450
00:36:37,508 --> 00:36:40,720
was not Gate 24, but the main terminal.

451
00:36:42,263 --> 00:36:46,726
They permitted her entry without detecting
the impersonation passport.

452
00:36:47,476 --> 00:36:48,894
No, well…

453
00:36:50,604 --> 00:36:54,942
-Anyway, if this becomes any bigger--
-We know.

454
00:36:55,026 --> 00:36:57,570
-Responsibility…
-Will be taken by me.

455
00:36:58,779 --> 00:37:02,366
Anyway, right now, we stop him.

456
00:37:03,451 --> 00:37:04,452
Contact the airport police.

457
00:37:04,535 --> 00:37:06,203
-Tell them about Takase!
-Okay!

458
00:37:24,847 --> 00:37:26,307
Takase.

459
00:37:27,224 --> 00:37:28,642
-Wait!
-Spotted Takase!

460
00:37:28,726 --> 00:37:29,643
Move!

461
00:37:29,727 --> 00:37:32,480
-Move! Move!
-Takase, stop!

462
00:37:33,147 --> 00:37:34,106
Stop!

463
00:37:35,232 --> 00:37:36,442
Takase!

464
00:37:41,989 --> 00:37:45,117
Announcement for passengers
on EuroSky Airways Flight

465
00:37:45,201 --> 00:37:48,496
ESA235 bound for London.

466
00:37:48,579 --> 00:37:51,582
The security checkpoint
is currently very crowded.

467
00:37:51,665 --> 00:37:53,250
-Jeez.
-Passengers boarding this flight,

468
00:37:53,334 --> 00:37:55,711
-I'm going.
-please complete security inspection early

469
00:37:55,795 --> 00:37:57,630
-and proceed to the gate.
-Wait!

470
00:37:58,589 --> 00:38:00,800
-Takase!
-There's nowhere to run!

471
00:38:11,143 --> 00:38:13,020
Stay back. I'll really do it.

472
00:38:13,104 --> 00:38:14,772
Takase, calm down.

473
00:38:14,855 --> 00:38:15,981
Shut up! Get back!

474
00:38:19,360 --> 00:38:20,736
Tsumugi!

475
00:38:21,695 --> 00:38:23,030
Dad!

476
00:38:24,615 --> 00:38:25,533
Dad?

477
00:38:33,332 --> 00:38:34,792
Takase.

478
00:38:37,294 --> 00:38:38,838
Let her go.

479
00:38:40,005 --> 00:38:43,050
Fukazawa, please let me go.

480
00:38:43,884 --> 00:38:47,555
I needed money!
I got into heavy debt at the casino!

481
00:38:48,222 --> 00:38:50,766
Back then, you saved me, didn't you?

482
00:38:50,850 --> 00:38:52,435
On the blizzard-covered mountain,

483
00:38:53,060 --> 00:38:54,895
you didn't abandon me!

484
00:38:54,979 --> 00:38:59,358
You know the weight of a life,
so why did you mess with it?

485
00:39:06,615 --> 00:39:09,076
Don't you dare desecrate life.

486
00:39:12,788 --> 00:39:14,331
Stay back!

487
00:39:34,977 --> 00:39:36,270
Secured!

488
00:39:39,440 --> 00:39:40,774
Oh my…

489
00:39:42,693 --> 00:39:43,986
They're good.

490
00:39:50,534 --> 00:39:52,495
Are you all right, Tsumugi?

491
00:39:54,371 --> 00:39:55,414
Not at all.

492
00:39:58,667 --> 00:40:00,920
You're late, Dad.

493
00:40:33,953 --> 00:40:35,329
Welcome home.

494
00:40:35,412 --> 00:40:37,623
Hello, dear.

495
00:40:38,207 --> 00:40:41,544
You're Misaki Takase, right?
Are you here to pick up your husband?

496
00:40:50,135 --> 00:40:53,055
-I'm glad you weren't injured.
-Yes.

497
00:40:53,138 --> 00:40:55,307
Though I did stomp on the culprit's foot.

498
00:40:55,391 --> 00:40:56,475
How reliable.

499
00:40:57,101 --> 00:40:58,519
Understood, thank you.

500
00:40:59,687 --> 00:41:01,689
If you head over right now,
you'll make it in time.

501
00:41:01,772 --> 00:41:03,816
I see. Thank you.

502
00:41:05,234 --> 00:41:07,861
-Well then, I'm off.
-Yes.

503
00:41:09,113 --> 00:41:11,448
Get along with Mom, okay?

504
00:41:11,532 --> 00:41:12,992
Don't worry.

505
00:41:13,742 --> 00:41:14,660
See you.

506
00:41:18,581 --> 00:41:19,582
Go ahead.

507
00:41:38,726 --> 00:41:41,729
Looks like you really are busy.

508
00:41:44,815 --> 00:41:46,483
See you, Inspector.

509
00:41:47,901 --> 00:41:50,863
-He's not an inspector, he's Chief--
-Forget it.

510
00:41:50,946 --> 00:41:51,864
See you.

511
00:41:54,408 --> 00:41:57,828
None of that stuff matters.

512
00:42:24,188 --> 00:42:27,983
The death certificate and cremation
certificate submitted by Takase

513
00:42:28,067 --> 00:42:29,943
were all forged.

514
00:42:30,027 --> 00:42:32,321
It seems the local doctor
was bribed as well.

515
00:42:33,155 --> 00:42:35,282
Going to such lengths…

516
00:42:35,366 --> 00:42:38,535
It seems the wife, Misaki, illegally
obtained another person's family register

517
00:42:38,619 --> 00:42:42,039
and returned to the country the day before
using a passport under that name.

518
00:42:42,122 --> 00:42:45,793
She intended to pretend she died
and live a new life as a different person.

519
00:42:47,544 --> 00:42:49,421
Regarding that urn,

520
00:42:49,505 --> 00:42:52,299
stimulant drugs were detected from inside.

521
00:42:52,383 --> 00:42:54,051
To evade inspection,

522
00:42:54,134 --> 00:42:56,553
it seems they placed human ash
at the top of the urn

523
00:42:56,637 --> 00:42:58,889
and hid the stimulant drugs underneath.

524
00:42:59,473 --> 00:43:03,018
Since what we tested was the ash
on top, no reaction came out.

525
00:43:03,102 --> 00:43:03,977
Yes.

526
00:43:04,061 --> 00:43:06,063
What was that ash, anyway?

527
00:43:06,146 --> 00:43:08,732
There is a high probability
it was animal bones.

528
00:43:09,983 --> 00:43:12,069
Really elaborate work.

529
00:43:13,070 --> 00:43:17,950
The reason we were able to figure it out
was thanks to Mori protecting the urn.

530
00:43:19,910 --> 00:43:23,580
Things are to be treated
with care, after all.

531
00:43:28,168 --> 00:43:32,005
Also, the two of them frequented
local underground casinos

532
00:43:32,089 --> 00:43:34,216
and accumulated large debts.

533
00:43:34,299 --> 00:43:38,137
It seems they were taken advantage of
and forced to work as couriers.

534
00:43:38,220 --> 00:43:41,682
The wife's death, the contents of the urn,

535
00:43:41,765 --> 00:43:44,143
it was all a lie.

536
00:43:45,227 --> 00:43:48,605
Objects do not tell lies.

537
00:43:53,527 --> 00:43:54,737
That's right.

538
00:43:55,904 --> 00:43:58,323
It's always humans who do.

539
00:44:06,081 --> 00:44:07,791
Good work, everyone.

540
00:44:07,875 --> 00:44:11,253
-It seems yesterday was quite hectic.
-This is business as usual.

541
00:44:12,504 --> 00:44:14,465
Today for sure, I'll get the inari sushi!

542
00:44:14,548 --> 00:44:17,092
I'm sorry. It's sold out today too.

543
00:44:17,176 --> 00:44:19,887
-What…
-It's remarkably popular, isn't it?

544
00:44:19,970 --> 00:44:22,181
The people over there ate all of it.

545
00:44:23,223 --> 00:44:24,349
Man…

546
00:44:28,854 --> 00:44:31,190
Ah, Mori, want some?

547
00:44:38,447 --> 00:44:39,698
Oh my…

548
00:44:44,286 --> 00:44:46,622
‎What is love?

549
00:44:46,705 --> 00:44:48,874
‎What, a fake proposal?

550
00:44:48,957 --> 00:44:49,833
‎Right here?

551
00:44:49,917 --> 00:44:52,461
‎-This guy is a marriage scammer!
‎-20 million yen.

552
00:44:52,544 --> 00:44:54,880
‎I will pay for all of it.

553
00:44:54,963 --> 00:44:56,715
‎What are these two?

554
00:44:56,798 --> 00:44:59,009
‎Inspecting love?

555
00:44:59,092 --> 00:44:59,968
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman

